1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,807
What if your shadow simply walked away?

2
00:00:02,847 --> 00:00:04,338
No warning, no goodbye.

3
00:00:04,378 --> 00:00:06,669
One second it's glued to your feet.

4
00:00:06,709 --> 00:00:09,665
The next, it's strolling down the street like

5
00:00:09,705 --> 00:00:11,197
it has somewhere to be.

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:13,473
You chase it.

7
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:14,659
It dodges a dog,

8
00:00:14,699 --> 00:00:16,288
tips an invisible hat,

9
00:00:16,328 --> 00:00:17,622
and buys a coffee.

10
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:20,660
Somehow a shadow holding a latte feels so

11
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:23,475
much worse than a shadow with no plan.

12
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,294
Then it catches the number nine bus.

13
00:00:27,334 --> 00:00:28,812
You catch your breath.

14
00:00:28,852 --> 00:00:31,987
Scientists say a shadow is only missing light,

15
00:00:32,027 --> 00:00:34,678
so hypothetically it cannot ride a bus.

16
00:00:34,718 --> 00:00:36,265
Nobody told the shadow.

17
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:37,868
Then word spreads.

18
00:00:37,908 --> 00:00:40,958
Across town, other shadows slip off their owners

19
00:00:40,998 --> 00:00:42,181
and join the march.

20
00:00:42,221 --> 00:00:43,403
Soon it's a parade,

21
00:00:43,443 --> 00:00:46,493
and thousands of people stand in plain sunlight,

22
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,166
feeling strangely exposed.

23
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:50,131
By sunset you give up.

24
00:00:50,171 --> 00:00:53,935
Without a shadow, bright afternoons feel weirdly empty,

25
00:00:53,975 --> 00:00:56,078
and every lamp post looks smug.

26
00:00:56,118 --> 00:00:57,807
You only want to go home,

27
00:00:57,847 --> 00:01:00,919
lock the door, and forget this ever happened.

28
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:03,736
You trudge home through the dark.

29
00:01:03,776 --> 00:01:05,024
And then you see it.

30
00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:07,408
Your living room light is already on.

31
00:01:07,448 --> 00:01:08,567
Someone is inside.

32
00:01:08,607 --> 00:01:11,466
A curtain twitches, and the silhouette waves.

33
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:14,856
Twist: the shadow got home first.

34
00:01:14,896 --> 00:01:16,530
It's wearing your slippers,

35
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:19,196
holding your keys, and it already made tea.

36
00:01:19,236 --> 00:01:20,560
It looks at the clock,

37
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,730
then at you, and says: you're late.

38
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:26,810
So whose shadow was it all along?

39
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:28,847
A thought experiment, of course.

40
00:01:28,887 --> 00:01:30,947
But tonight, glance at the floor.

41
00:01:30,987 --> 00:01:33,047
Maybe it was never following you.

42
00:01:33,087 --> 00:01:36,038
Maybe it was just waiting for you to come home.
